---
import ToyboxLayout from "../../../layouts/ToyboxLayout.astro"
---

<ToyboxLayout
	title="k8's corner - toybox/ltd texture editor"
	description="edit ugc textures from tomodachi life: living the dream"
>
	<p>
		so far it can only load the image Lmfao I'll add the actual editing part
		later maybe possibly 😭
	</p>
	<div
		style="display: flex; justify-content: center; align-items: center; padding: 1em;"
	>
		<canvas
			id="texture-canvas"
			style="size: 512px !important; height: 512px !important; aspect-ratio: 1/1; image-rendering: pixelated; display: block;"
			class="border"
		>
		</canvas>
	</div>

	<p>DOOHICKEY STATUS: <span id="status">Feed me canvasesssss</span></p>

	<p>upload a .canvas.zs file here</p>
	<input type="file" id="file-input" accept=".zs" />
	<button class="card" id="reload">Reload image</button>
	<form>
		<label for="swizzle-mode">Swizzle mode (4 for full canvases)</label>
		<input
			type="range"
			id="swizzle-mode"
			name="swizzle-mode"
			min="0"
			max="10"
			value="4"
			oninput="this.nextElementSibling.value = this.value"
		/>
		<output>4</output>

		<br />

		<label for="width">Width</label>
		<input
			type="number"
			id="width"
			name="width"
			min="2"
			max="1024"
			value="256"
			placeholder="256"
		/>

		<br />

		<label for="height">Height</label>
		<input
			type="number"
			id="height"
			name="height"
			min="2"
			max="1024"
			value="256"
			placeholder="256"
		/>
		<br />

		<label for="width">Block Width</label>
		<input
			type="number"
			id="block-width"
			name="block-width"
			min="1"
			max="1024"
			value="1"
			placeholder="1"
		/>

		<br />

		<label for="height">Block Height</label>
		<input
			type="number"
			id="block-height"
			name="block-height"
			min="1"
			max="1024"
			value="1"
			placeholder="1"
		/>
		<br />

		<label for="height">Bytes per block</label>
		<input
			type="number"
			id="bytes-per-block"
			name="bytes-per-block"
			min="1"
			value="4"
			placeholder="4"
		/>
		<br />
		<button class="card" type="submit">OK</button>
	</form>

	<h1>general info about this tool</h1>
	<h3><span>.canvas.zs</span> format</h3>
	<p>
		tomodachi life saves UGC drawings in a .canvas file compressed with
		zstandard. decompressing the file will yield the 256x256 canvas, which is
		just 65536 bytes representing RGBA pixels. however, the game "swizzles" this
		canvas, which is to rearrange it into a format that's more performant on the
		switch's GPU.
	</p>
	<p>
		in order to assemble an actual image, we need to reassemble the image from
		the swizzled format. <a href="https://github.com/Aclios/pyswizzle"
			>pyswizzle</a
		> implements all the logic for this, and also includes an additional mode for
		swizzled graphics from PS4 games. check it out!
	</p>
	<p>
		pyswizzle was partially reimplemented in javascript, but only limited to the
		scope of the switch's swizzling for this tool.
	</p>
	<h3>organization of the UGC drawings</h3>
	<p>
		UGC drawings are saved in the order they're created, and separated into
		categories by filename.
	</p>
	<p>
		they take the format <span>Ugc[category][num].canvas.zs</span>, where <span
			>[category]</span
		> is the type of the item, such as <span>Food</span> for food or <span
			>Goods</span
		> for treasures. <span>[num]</span> is the order of its creation, starting from
		<span>000</span> and incrementing by 1 until the cap of the item type is reached.
	</p>
	<p>
		i'm not quite sure what the <span>.ugctex</span> files do, but they seem to be
		something to do with lighting?
	</p>

	<hr />

	<p>
		"Tomodachi Life" is a registered trademark of Nintendo Co., Ltd, which is
		not affiliated with, and does not endorse, this tool or website.
	</p>

	<p>
		Based on the work of Aclios' <a href="https://github.com/Aclios/pyswizzle"
			>pyswizzle</a
		>
	</p>

	<script>
		// @ts-nocheck
		import * as fzstd from "fzstd"
		import BytesDeswizzler from "./swizzler.js"

		const canvas = document.getElementById("texture-canvas")
		const uploader = document.getElementById("file-input")
		const ctx = canvas.getContext("2d")
		const status = document.getElementById("status")

		var width = 256
		var height = 256
		var blockSize = [1, 1]
		var bytesPerBlock = 4
		var swizzleMode = 4

		let lastCanvas = undefined

		const form = document.querySelector("form")

		if (form) {
			form.addEventListener("submit", (event) => {
				event.preventDefault()
				console.log(form.elements)
				width = form.elements["width"].value
				height = form.elements["height"].value
				blockSize = [
					form.elements["block-width"].value,
					form.elements["block-height"].value,
				]
				bytesPerBlock = form.elements["bytes-per-block"].value
				swizzleMode = form.elements["swizzle-mode"].value
                status.innerText = "Reconfigured"
			})
		}

		function reloadCanvas() {
			try {
				status.innerText = "Reloading canvas"
				loadCanvas(lastCanvas)
			} catch (e) {
				console.error("Reloading canvas failed:", e.message)
				status.innerText = "Reloading canvas failed: " + e.message
			}
		}

		function loadCanvas(decompressedBytes) {
			canvas.width = width
			canvas.height = height
			status.innerText = "Deswizzling"
			const deswizzler = new BytesDeswizzler(
				decompressedBytes,
				[width, height],
				blockSize,
				bytesPerBlock,
				swizzleMode,
			)

			const deswizzledRaw = deswizzler.deswizzle()

			// Final render
			status.innerText = "Drawing"
			const clampedArray = new Uint8ClampedArray(deswizzledRaw)
			const imageData = new ImageData(clampedArray, width, height)
			ctx.putImageData(imageData, 0, 0)
			status.innerText = "Done!"
		}

		uploader.addEventListener("change", async (event) => {
			const file = event.target.files[0]
			if (!file) return
			try {
				status.innerText = "Reading in file"
				const buffer = await file.arrayBuffer()
				status.innerText = "Decompressing canvas"
				const decompressed = fzstd.decompress(new Uint8Array(buffer))
				lastCanvas = decompressed
				loadCanvas(decompressed)
			} catch (e) {
				console.error("Loading canvas failed:", e.message)
				status.innerText = "Loading canvas failed: " + e.message
			}
		})

        document.getElementById("reload").onclick = reloadCanvas
	</script>
</ToyboxLayout>
